      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    stock_price = 150.0\n    strike_price = 160.0\n    time_to_expiration = 0.5\n    risk_free_rate = 0.05\n    volatility = 0.20\n\n    # Calculate d1 and d2\n    import math\n\n    d1 = (\n        math.log(stock_price / strike_price)\n        + (risk_free_rate + 0.5 * volatility ** 2) * time_to_expiration\n    ) / (volatility * math.sqrt(time_to_expiration))\n\n    d2 = d1 - volatility * math.sqrt(time_to_expiration)\n\n    # Standard normal cumulative distribution function\n    def norm_cdf(x):\n        return 0.5 * (1 + math.erf(x / math.sqrt(2)))\n\n    # Calculate the Black-Scholes call option price\n    call_price = (\n        stock_price * norm_cdf(d1)\n        - strike_price\n        * math.exp(-risk_free_rate * time_to_expiration)\n        * norm_cdf(d2)\n    )\n\n    # Return the price rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(call_price, 2)\n```",
